  message: "SAME SHAPE IN THREE MORE LANGUAGES, for whoever fixes this (WI-vafad tranche 3, 2026-10-03, docs/audits/0022):\n- objc NSFileHandle `seekToFileOffset:` and swift FileHandle `seekToEnd` are rowed fs_write. The tranche-2 flags were re-verified ACCEPT by the tranche-3 verifier: seek(toFileOffset:) -> lseek(SEEK_SET) only, and seekToEnd is lseek(_fd, 0, SEEK_END) returning the offset (swift-corelibs-foundation FileHandle.swift:583, :566-568, a reimplementation). No byte moves. The swift / objc write methods stay rowed.\n- haskell.yaml:133 rows hSeek / hTell / hIsEOF / hReady / hFileSize under fs_read. These are vouched rows outside the sweep's scope and NOT adjudicated; named so the family is complete.\nOne rule across languages (\"a stream-position call crosses nothing\", rust.yaml:70 / :186's wording) is better than five per-language decisions. The ADR-0049 ruling-3 proof still runs per language."  # 4917
